Build fix of CalculiX 2.23 for the mingw-w64 UCRT toolchain (GPL-2.0, like CalculiX itself). Applied by installer/windows/build_ccx.sh with
`patch -p1` in the folder that contains CalculiX/ccx_2.23/.

Both files begin with an old-style declaration at file scope (NOT a call - nothing is executed):

    #ifdef __WIN32
    _set_output_format(_TWO_DIGIT_EXPONENT);
    #endif

that the old MSVCRT headers accepted as an implicit-int declaration. With the UCRT headers of the current mingw-w64 the line is an error (the
function is declared with a prototype in <stdio.h>, and gcc 14+ rejects a declaration without parameter types). The UCRT always prints exponents
with two digits at least, which is what the line was meant to ensure for the old runtime. No solver code is changed.

--- a/CalculiX/ccx_2.23/src/ccx_2.23.c
+++ b/CalculiX/ccx_2.23/src/ccx_2.23.c
@@ -16,7 +16,6 @@
 /*     Foundation, Inc., 675 Mass Ave, Cambridge, MA 02139, USA.         */

 #ifdef __WIN32
-_set_output_format(_TWO_DIGIT_EXPONENT);
 #endif

 #ifdef CALCULIX_MPI
--- a/CalculiX/ccx_2.23/src/ccx_2.23step.c
+++ b/CalculiX/ccx_2.23/src/ccx_2.23step.c
@@ -16,7 +16,6 @@
 /*     Foundation, Inc., 675 Mass Ave, Cambridge, MA 02139, USA.         */

 #ifdef __WIN32
-_set_output_format(_TWO_DIGIT_EXPONENT);
 #endif

 #ifdef CALCULIX_MPI
